-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/49ea1d59-3ac9-5777-956f-feaa1311bcc3
-- title:
--   Basic properties of the blow-up chart C[J/a] at an end
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $5 \le q$, $M'$ a non-zero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, $\ell$ a prime with $3 \le \ell$, $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$, $L$ a field of characteristic zero and $\xi \in L$ a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity; the hypothesis `hι` asks for a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota \xi = \exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$.
--
--   The field $K$ is an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$, and `hK` identifies it with [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M'))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103): the $L$-subfield of $L((t))$ generated by the coefficientwise image under $\mathbb{Q} \to L$ of the $q$-expansion function field over $\mathbb{Q}$ of the congruence subgroup attached to the level $N_0 = (q\ell)^2 M'$ and the subgroup $H =$ `levelH (q*ℓ) M'`, the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/N_0)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times$, that is the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell$. The ring $A$ is a Henselian discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$ and algebraically closed residue field, with $q \in \mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hAq`) and $\xi$ in the image of $A$ (`hξA`), equipped with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $L$; $\varpi$ generates $\mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hϖ`), and $\varpi_t \in A$ satisfies $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q u$ for a unit $u$ (`hϖt`). The element $j \in K$ is non-zero and its Laurent expansion is the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the $j$-function (`hj`).
--
--   Write $C =$ `chartAlgFin A K j` for the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ consisting of the elements integral over $A[j]$, and $X =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) for the scheme obtained as the pushout gluing $\mathrm{Spec}\,C$ to the corresponding chart built from $j^{-1}$, with structure morphism `toBase` to $\mathrm{Spec}\,A$ and with $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}} : \mathrm{Spec}\,C \to X$. The ideal $y \subset C$ is maximal (`hy`) and contains $\varpi$ (`hϖy`), and `hss` is the supersingularity condition at $y$: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), i.e. every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $\varphi(j)$ has no non-zero point killed by $q$.
--
--   The hypothesis `hArig` (the Drinfeld-chart witness hypothesis, quantified over all ends) requires, for every point $z$ of $X$ such that the germ at $z$ of the global section $\varpi$ pulled back from $\mathrm{Spec}\,A$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$, and every point $y'$ of $\mathrm{Spec}\,C$ with $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}(y') = z$ whose ideal satisfies the same supersingularity condition as $y$: the existence of a complete discrete valuation ring $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ with $\mathfrak{m}_W = (\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f, u, v \in W[[X_0, X_1]]$ with $u, v$ units and $f \equiv X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ (the Drinfeld form [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18)), and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ onto $S = W[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{q+1}))v - fu)$, subject to the following clauses, whose content is summarised here: (a) $e$ carries the germ of a constant $a \in A$ to the class of $C(\sigma a)$; (b) for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ every $L$-automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ which is a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ in the sense of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) (that is, for all weights $k$, all modular forms $f, g$ of level $\Gamma_H(N_0,H)$ with integral $q$-expansions and $g \ne 0$, and all $x \in K$ whose Laurent expansion is that of $f/g$, the complex expansion of $\tau x$ times the $q$-expansion of $g\mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,(q\ell)\,\gamma^{-1}$ equals the $q$-expansion of $f\mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,(q\ell)\,\gamma^{-1}$) preserves $C$; (c) if moreover $\gamma \in \Gamma(\ell)$, the induced endomorphism of $C$ is congruent to the identity modulo $y'$; (d) for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and such a $\tau$ preserving $C$ and congruent to the identity modulo $y'$, there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c \in W$ and a matrix $M \in M_2(W)$ such that $\theta$ intertwines $e$ composed with the completion of the germ map $C \to \mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ with the corresponding map for $\tau|_C$, $\theta$ fixes the classes of constants, $\theta(X_j) \equiv \sum_i M_{ij}X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by the classes of $X_0, X_1$, $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$ and $M \equiv c\gamma$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$, $c \equiv 1$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(\ell)$, and $c \not\equiv 1$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \ne \mathrm{id}$; (e) two primes $P_1, P_2$ of $S$, each not containing both classes of $X_0$ and $X_1$ and each containing the class of $C(\sigma\varpi)$, which carry tangent forms $a_1X_0 + b_1X_1$ and $a_2X_0 + b_2X_1$ (modulo $(X_0,X_1)^2$) with $q \nmid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$, have distinct contractions to $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$; (f) for such a prime $P$ with tangent form $X_0$, an element $a \in C$ has its germ in the contraction of $P$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak{m}_A$; (g) the element [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $K$ and in $C$, and there are $a_0 \in A$ with that element congruent to $a_0$ modulo $y'$, an integer $e_0 \ge 1$ and $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ whose degree-$e_0$ form is a unit at every $(a,b) \in W^2$ not both in $\mathfrak{m}_W$ with $a^qb - ab^q \in \mathfrak{m}_W$, such that $e$ sends the germ of that element minus $a_0$ to the class of $h$.
--
--   Next a particular end is fixed: a point $z$ of $X$, the germ $\varpi z$ of $\varpi$ at $z$ (`hϖz`) lying in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ (`hz`), a point $y'$ of $\mathrm{Spec}\,C$ with $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}(y') = z$ (`hy'`) satisfying the supersingularity condition (`hss'`) and with $y' = y$ as ideals of $C$ (`hy'y`); and a witness for this end: a complete discrete valuation ring $W_1$, a homomorphism $\sigma_1 : A \to W_1$ with $\mathfrak{m}_{W_1} = (\sigma_1\varpi)$ (`hσ₁`), series $f_1, u_1, v_1$ with $u_1, v_1$ units (`hu₁`, `hv₁`) and $f_1$ congruent to the Drinfeld form modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ (`hf₁`), and an isomorphism $e_1$ from the adic completion of $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ onto $S = W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{q+1}))v_1 - f_1u_1)$. The hypothesis `hW₁` asserts for this fixed witness exactly the clauses (a)–(g) listed above, with $W_1, \sigma_1, f_1, u_1, v_1, e_1$ in place of $W, \sigma, f, u, v, e$.
--
--   The ideal $J \subseteq C$ is, by `hJ`, the infimum of the set of those ideals of $C$ of the form: the contraction along the restriction to $C$ of a level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$, with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$, of the contraction along $e_1$ composed with the completed germ map of the ideal of $S$ generated by the classes of $C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)$, $X_0$ and $X_1$. The $A$-subalgebra $B \subseteq K$ is, by `hB`, generated over $C$ by all $x \in K$ with $x\varpi_t \in J$, that is $B = C[J/\varpi_t]$. Further, $\mathcal{W}$ is a valuation subring of $K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`), and four groups of hypotheses are imposed on this configuration: `hR1` says $C \subseteq B$ and every $f \in K$ is a quotient $g/h$ with $g, h \in B$, $h \ne 0$; `hR2` says $A \to B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation and $B/(\varpi)$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; `hR3` (five clauses) says that an element of $L$ lies in $\mathcal{W}$ exactly when it comes from $A$, that $\mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{W}}$ is generated by $\varpi$, that $\mathcal{W}$ is a discrete valuation ring, that an element of $C$ lies in $y$ exactly when it lies in $\mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{W}}$, and that $\mathcal{W}$ is the localisation of $B$ outside $\mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{W}}$; `hEQ` (five clauses, summarised here) provides, for every $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field of $A$, a surjection $\rho$ from $B$ onto the Drinfeld coordinate ring [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q (ResidueField A)`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) with kernel $\mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{W}} \cap B$, compatible with $A \to \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ and equivariant for level automorphisms through [`DrinfeldCurve.hAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L325) via a scalar $c$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, c) \in$ [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) and $c \ne 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \ne \mathrm{id}$; that $B$ is stable under all level automorphisms at $\gamma^{-1}$ for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; that every prime of $B$ containing $\varpi$ receives $\mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{W}} \cap B$ under some level automorphism with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$; that an element of $B$ sent into $\mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{W}}$ by all such automorphisms is divisible by $\varpi$; and that a level automorphism preserving $y$ preserves $\mathcal{W}$.
--
--   Finally, `hjK` and `hjC` record that [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $K$ and in $C$; $m \ge 1$ is an integer with $\varpi^m = \varpi_t w$ for a unit $w$ (`hm1`, `hmt`); $a \in C$ lies in $J$ (`haJ`) and is non-zero in $K$ (`ha0`); the $A$-subalgebra $B_a \subseteq K$ is generated over $C$ by all $x \in K$ with $xa \in J$, that is $B_a = C[J/a]$ (`hBa`); $P$ is a maximal ideal of $B_a$ (`hP`); $\mathcal{O}$ is a subring of $K$ with $f \in \mathcal{O}$ if and only if $f = g/h$ for some $g, h \in B_a$ with $h \notin P$ (`hOdef`), so that $\mathcal{O}$ is the localisation of $B_a$ at $P$ inside $K$; every element of $y$ which lies in $\mathcal{O}$ is a non-unit of $\mathcal{O}$ (`hOy`); and $B$ is not contained in $\mathcal{O}$ (`hOB`).
--
--   Under these hypotheses the conclusion is the conjunction of six assertions: $B_a$ is a Noetherian ring; every element of $C$ lies in $B_a$; for $b \in C$ whose image in $K$ lies in $B_a$, that image lies in $P$ if and only if $b \in y$; for every $f \in \mathcal{O}$ there is $a' \in A$ whose image in $K$ lies in $\mathcal{O}$ and such that $f - a'$ is not a unit of $\mathcal{O}$; the element $\varpi_t a^{-1}$ of $K$ lies in $B_a$ and lies in $P$; and $i a^{-1} \in B_a$ for every $i \in J$.
--
--   This is the elementary algebra of an affine chart $B_a = C[J/a]$ at an end of the blow-up of the supersingular chart $C$ along the weighted centre $J$, together with the identification of its closed point: $P$ cuts out $y$ on $C$, the local ring $\mathcal{O} = (B_a)_P$ has residues in $A$, and $\varpi_t/a$ lies in $P$, which is the precise sense in which the end is disjoint from the $\varpi_t$-chart $B$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_ringHom_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_uvCrossingModel_coeff_tangent_centre_of_end_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_ringHom_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_uvCrossingModel_coeff_tangent_centre_of_end_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked), where the completion of $\mathcal{O}$ is put in crossing form.
